## Original Content
The primary runoff in South Carolina between Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman is another test of President Trump's influence. He's backing Darline, sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.

## Summary
The South Carolina U.S. Senate primary runoff election between Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman serves as a test of President Trump's political influence, with Trump endorsing Darline Graham, sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.

## Key Points
- The election is a primary runoff in South Carolina.
- Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman are the candidates.
- President Trump is endorsing Darline Graham.
- This election is seen as a test of Trump's endorsement power.


